From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: compact reports and recycled fence lists (EDEN_UP_REPORT_NO_ALLOC)

DRAFT, not built. Ports Frizti/Fritchii 112ba4d (@Frizti) and the report part of
zortos293/Lichii PR #1161, 792e12a47b (@lucastaonline). Gated by EDEN_UP_REPORT_NO_ALLOC (exact
1), read once at boot (not a live switch: the free query-ID FIFOs are mode-specific); off by
default. Independent of 0557-0559. On: cleared fence operation lists are recycled (up to 32), free
query IDs use a vector/head FIFO, reports use a trivial 16-byte callable that looks up guest
pointers after FinishReads, dead-bank host query resets go to the Vulkan worker, the equal-tick
semaphore CAS is skipped, and report pages outside the read-back extrema skip the buffer cache
lock. The on boot logs "EDEN_UP_REPORT_NO_ALLOC=1: compact reports and recycled fence lists".
The matching tools/check-fence-requirements.py change lands in the front tree in the same commit.

Reviewed draft from job J, v2: reviewer re-anchored the vk_rasterizer.cpp include hunk, kept the
fence operation lists std::deque in both modes (the draft made them std::vector even when off),
dropped the reserve(64) on the on path, and adapted check-fence-requirements.py's mocks to deque.
